{
 "spec_version": "2.3.0",
 "about": "RescueCodec domain frame vectors (SPEC section 3.8, first byte 0x03). vocabularies: id, domain, code width and SHA-256 of each bundled vocabulary file; check them. frames: encode_domain(text, vocab) must give hex exactly and decode_domain(hex) must give decoded (decode_any adds \"v\": 2). trace is informative (one line per code). streams: encode_stream(text, vocab) must give stream exactly and decode_stream(stream, vocab) must give text (no frame, may be larger than one packet). random: like streams, seeded random texts. invalid_decode: decode_domain(hex) must be rejected with error. invalid_encode: encode_domain(text, vocab) must be rejected with error. unknown: decode_domain(hex) must give decoded ({\"unknown\": {\"vocab\": id}}), rendered as render.en. choice: the send rule (SPEC 2.3 rule 6, 3.8.6) for {\"id\": 3, \"text\": {\"text\": text}} in a chat that packs, compact text on, team vocabulary setting: form, vocab, size and hex of what goes out; sizes lists the candidates (DEFLATE is left out: compressors may differ, and in these cases it is at least 3 bytes larger than what goes out).",
